Vulnerability Title

Broken Access Control via Direct Object Reference Allowing Unauthorized Access to Business Definition Details

Vulnerability Category
Authorization Vulnerability
Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR)
Broken Access Control
OWASP Category (OWASP Top 10 – 2021 / 2025 Mapping)
A01: Broken Access Control
CVSS v4.0 Score

CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:H/SI:L/SA:N
Base Score: 8.7 (High)

If the data is highly confidential or regulated, the severity may increase depending on business impact.

Description

The application exposes Business Definition Details through a direct URL endpoint without properly validating user authorization and entitlement checks on the server side.

Although access to the Business Definition Details page is restricted in the user interface based on user entitlements, an authenticated user without the required permissions can directly access sensitive business information by manually modifying or invoking the backend URL/API endpoint.

This indicates that authorization controls are enforced only at the UI level and not properly validated server-side.

An attacker with a low-privileged account can bypass intended access restrictions and retrieve sensitive business definition information belonging to other users or business units.

Impact

Successful exploitation of this vulnerability may allow unauthorized users to:

Access sensitive business definition details without proper entitlement
Bypass role-based access control (RBAC) restrictions
Enumerate internal business configurations and metadata
Access confidential business logic or operational information
Facilitate further attacks using exposed internal data
Violate compliance and data segregation requirements

Depending on the sensitivity of the exposed data, this vulnerability could lead to:

Information disclosure
Privilege abuse
Unauthorized business intelligence access
Regulatory and compliance risks
Mitigation

The application should enforce authorization validation on the server side for every request accessing Business Definition Details.

Recommended remediations:

Implement strict server-side access control checks for all sensitive endpoints.
Validate user entitlements and roles before returning business definition data.
Avoid relying solely on UI-based restrictions for authorization enforcement.
Implement object-level authorization validation for every resource request.
Use centralized authorization middleware/framework controls.
Log and monitor unauthorized access attempts.
Perform periodic access control testing and secure code reviews.
