Vulnerability Title

Verbose Error Message and Stack Trace Disclosure Leading to Information Exposure

Vulnerability Category
Information Disclosure
Improper Error Handling
Stack Trace Disclosure
OWASP Category (OWASP Top 10 – 2021 / 2025 Mapping)
A05: Security Misconfiguration
A01: Broken Access Control (if internal functions/endpoints become discoverable and exploitable)
CVSS v4.0 Score

CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:N/SA:N
Base Score: 5.3 (Medium)

Description

The application discloses detailed internal error messages and full stack traces when processing malformed or unexpected user input.

During testing, the application returned an HTTP 500 Internal Server Error page containing:

Internal Java exception details
Full stack trace information
Framework and library names
Internal package structure
Source file names and line numbers
Controller method names

Observed details include:

java.lang.NumberFormatException
ClientProfileController.searchTNL
Internal Spring Framework classes
Apache Tomcat server information

The error page reveals sensitive backend implementation details that should not be exposed to end users.

This vulnerability occurs due to improper exception handling and insecure server configuration.

Impact

An attacker may leverage the disclosed information to:

Identify backend technologies and frameworks
Map internal application architecture
Discover internal classes, methods, and endpoints
Assist in crafting targeted attacks
Facilitate exploitation of other vulnerabilities
Gain insights into input validation weaknesses

Verbose error messages significantly reduce the effort required for reconnaissance and application fingerprinting.

Mitigation
Disable detailed error messages and stack traces in production environments.
Implement centralized exception handling mechanisms.
Configure custom generic error pages for HTTP 4xx and 5xx responses.
Avoid exposing:
Source code references
Internal package names
File paths
Stack traces
Framework versions
Log detailed exceptions only on the server side.
Configure Spring/Tomcat securely:
Disable debug mode
Suppress stack trace rendering
Implement proper input validation to prevent unhandled exceptions.

Example generic response:

“An unexpected error occurred. Please contact support.”

Evidence Observed

The application returned:

HTTP Status 500 – Internal Server Error
java.lang.NumberFormatException
ClientProfileController.java:177
Spring Framework stack trace
Apache Tomcat server disclosure
